Done in "[PATCH 0/2] libexec/mail: Deliver only mail messages" [1].
maildir-deliver.sh is the program git send-email would call, and it
now refuses input that is not a message. That means malformed headers,
no empty line after them, or anything other than exactly one From,
Subject, and Message-ID. A refused message never reaches the maildir.
All 30 recent list messages I tried still pass, and so does a git
format-patch series. The first patch fixes the patch-triage skill,
which composed its report without a From or a Message-ID.

Under your lab-mail design below, agents would hand mail to lab-mail
over SMTP, so they could not get around a check in their own jail.
[inference, from smtpd.conf(5)] OpenSMTPD can run the same script as
its delivery agent ("action ... mda"), so the check and the
